  "review_notes": [
    "A competing reading fuses `יִּשָּׂא` and `פְּנֵי` into one *accepted* unit; the intervening subject and object marker defeat rule 30's contiguity condition, which is why the split was taken here while the contiguous `פָּנָיו אֶשָּׂא` of v8 was fused.",
    "`כַּאֲשֶׁר` was split across *according as*; a fused reading is available but the ASV spends a word on each morpheme."
